From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:33:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 78/93] dt-bindings: display: apple,dcp: add apple,secure-mbox

The boot loader hands the display over only to a node whose mboxes is
the one ASC mailbox. A machine whose internal DCP has a secure port
names it in a property of its own there, and the driver takes it as the
"secure" mailbox.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>

[re-cut onto the K114s r3d tree]
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
index 171c49cd125..b06974140da 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
@@ -94,6 +94,14 @@ properties:
       - const: mbox
       - const: secure
 
+  apple,secure-mbox:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      The coprocessor's secure RTBuddy port, on a machine whose boot loader
+      hands the display over only to a node with a single mailbox in mboxes.
+      The driver takes it as the "secure" mailbox. Elsewhere the port is the
+      second entry of mboxes.
+
   iommus:
     maxItems: 1
 
